  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral humanitarian assistance to vulnerable groups of people affected by the Ukraine war, in Ukraine and surrounding countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved wellbeing and dignity of vulnerable groups, including older people, persons with disabilities and their carers affected by the conflict in Ukraine</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program will specifically address the identified needs and risks faced by older people, including older women and those with disabilities in Ukraine and bordering countries</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program will specifically address the identified needs and risks faced by older people, including older women and those with disabilities in Ukraine and bordering countries, by providing psychological support to older people affected by the conflict through a case management approach of Home-Based Care (HBC) (whether at home or displaced), Community Safe Space (CSS) activities in locations where internally displaced people (IDPs) are residing and the provision of personalised assistance, through basic hygiene items and provision of assistive products as well as targeted multi-purpose cash assistance (MPCA).</narrative>
  </description>
